{"toolCallId":"call_42d7fab08b804e2486a6e11295c3c9f0","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"[\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"FILE_EXISTS\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"FILES\",\n      \"FILES_PRESENT\",\n      \"FILES_EXISTS\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-files.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Validates required spec documents for the declared documentation level.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"PLACEHOLDER_FILLED\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"PLACEHOLDER\",\n      \"PLACEHOLDERS\",\n      \"PLACEHOLDERS_FILLED\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-placeholders.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Rejects unfilled template placeholders in authored spec documents.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"COMMENT_HYGIENE_MARKER\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"COMMENT_HYGIENE\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-comment-hygiene.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Rejects ephemeral finding markers inside HTML comments in authored spec documents.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"SCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"SCAFFOLD_MARKERS\",\n      \"TEMPLATE_SCAFFOLD\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-scaffold-never-touched.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Rejects scaffold-signature markers in required docs when spec.md claims Complete status.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"STATUS_CROSS_DOC_CONSISTENCY\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"STATUS_CONSISTENCY\",\n      \"CROSS_DOC_STATUS\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-status-cross-doc-consistency.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Advisory-by-default check that spec.md and implementation-summary.md status fields classify to the same delivery state.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"LEVEL_DECLARED\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"LEVEL\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-level.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"info\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Reports whether the documentation level was declared or inferred.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"AC_COVERAGE\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"ACCEPTANCE_COVERAGE\",\n      \"AC_TRACEABILITY\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-ac-coverage.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"info\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"flags\": [\n      \"SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE\",\n      \"SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_ENFORCE\",\n      \"SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_FLOOR\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Default-on advisory (non-blocking) scan for acceptance-criteria traceability coverage; set SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=false to opt out.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"AC_CLOSURE\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"ACCEPTANCE_CLOSURE\",\n      \"AC_GATE\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-ac-closure.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"flags\": [\n      \"SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE\",\n      \"SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Gates packet closure on acceptance-criteria.md at Levels 2, 3 and 3+; unmet criteria block a completion claim and a waiver must cite an ADR that exists. Packets created before the cutoff stay advisory.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"ANCHORS_VALID\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"ANCHOR\",\n      \"ANCHORS\",\n      \"ANCHOR_MATCHED\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"native:orchestrator\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks anchors in each spec doc whose template defines them, ignoring fenced code; a phase parent is exempt, and research/research.md and review/review-report.md are skipped as free-form workflow documents. Errors: a doc with no anchors, an anchor opened twice, never closed, closed but never opened, or closed more times than it is opened. Nesting is also an error: an anchor opened inside another, closed before it is opened, or closed while another is still open, though markers quoted in inline code are ignored by the nesting check; an adr-NNN anchor may hold adr-NNN-* anchors. Template order is not checked.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"FRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"MEMORY_BLOCK\",\n      \"FRONTMATTER_MEMORY\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"ts:spec-doc-structure\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Validates canonical _memory continuity frontmatter blocks.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"MERGE_LEGALITY\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"MERGE\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"ts:spec-doc-structure\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Validates generated merge payloads against target anchor shape.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"SUFFICIENCY\",\n      \"DOC_SUFFICIENCY\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"ts:spec-doc-structure\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks implementation-summary sufficiency after save/write flows.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"CROSS_ANCHOR_CONTAMINATION\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"CONTAMINATION\",\n      \"CROSS_ANCHOR\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"ts:spec-doc-structure\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Detects route/category mismatches before generated content is merged.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"POST_SAVE_FINGERPRINT\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"FINGERPRINT\",\n      \"POST_SAVE\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"ts:spec-doc-structure\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Verifies post-save fingerprints for generated writes.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"TOC_POLICY\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"TOC\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-toc-policy.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Enforces table-of-contents placement policy.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"AI_PROTOCOLS\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"AI_PROTOCOL\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-ai-protocols.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Validates AI execution protocol sections in high-governance specs.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"COMPLEXITY_MATCH\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"COMPLEXITY\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-complexity.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks declared level against content complexity signals.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"FOLDER_NAMING\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-folder-naming.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Validates numbered spec-folder naming conventions.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"FRONTMATTER_VALID\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"FRONTMATTER\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-frontmatter.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Validates YAML frontmatter structure and required semantic values.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"FRONTMATTER_VALUES\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"FRONTMATTER_VALUE_LIST\",\n      \"CONTEXT_TYPE_VALUES\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-frontmatter-values.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"warn\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Warns when a packet document's contextType or importance_tier is outside the shared list in sk-doc/sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-values.json. Aliases are legal.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"SOURCE_TAGS\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"SOURCE_TAG_RESOLVER\",\n      \"SOURCE_CITATIONS\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-source-tags.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"warn\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"flags\": [\n      \"SPECKIT_SOURCE_TAG_CUTOFF\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Warns when a path:line citation inside a [SOURCE: ...] tag in a packet's research or review artifacts names a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, using sk-doc's citation resolver. Packets created on or before the cutoff are skipped. A pass means the path and line exist, not that they support the claim.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"GREP_CONVENTION\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"GREP\",\n      \"GREPPABLE\",\n      \"RETRIEVAL_CONVENTION\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-grep-convention.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks every markdown document in a spec folder against the greppable-corpus convention: frontmatter variant, trigger phrase quality, anchor grammar and naming.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"LEVEL_MATCH\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-level-match.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks required files match the declared documentation level.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"GRAPH_METADATA_PRESENT\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"GRAPH_METADATA\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-graph-metadata.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"warn\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks generated description and graph metadata are present.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_DRIFT\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"CHILD_DRIFT\",\n      \"GRAPH_CHILD_DRIFT\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-graph-metadata-child-drift.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"warn\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Flags graph-metadata.json children_ids missing on-disk phase children the writer would add (advisory unless SPECKIT_CHILD_DRIFT_ENFORCE=true).\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_IDENTITY\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"CHILD_IDENTITY\",\n      \"GRAPH_CHILD_IDENTITY\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-graph-metadata-child-identity.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"structural\",\n    \"description\": \"Flags graph-metadata.json children_ids entries whose leading path identity is not the packet's own current identity (stale rename residue the refresh writer now prunes).\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"GRAPH_SHAPE\",\n      \"GRAPH_METADATA_VALID\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-graph-metadata-shape.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"warn\",\n    \"category\": \"structural\",\n    \"description\": \"Validates graph-metadata.json shape: required packet/derived blocks, last_active_child_id pointer integrity for phase parents.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"METADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"METADATA_DISK_CONSISTENCY\",\n      \"DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-metadata-disk-consistency.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"structural\",\n    \"description\": \"Advisory-by-default check that description.json, graph-metadata.json, and continuity ids match the real on-disk spec-folder path.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"DESCRIPTION_SHAPE\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"DESC_SHAPE\",\n      \"DESCRIPTION_VALID\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-description-shape.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"warn\",\n    \"category\": \"structural\",\n    \"description\": \"Validates description.json shape: required name/description/level keys present and well-typed.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"NORMALIZER_LINT\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"NORMALIZER\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-normalizer-lint.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Strict-only lint for duplicated runtime normalizer helpers.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"DOC_INTEGRITY\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-spec-doc-integrity.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Verifies inline markdown references resolve within spec docs.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"TEMPLATE_SOURCE\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-template-source.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"authored_template\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE provenance markers.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"CANONICAL_SAVE_ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-canonical-save-root-spec.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Ensures canonical saves include a root spec reference.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"CANONICAL_SAVE_SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-canonical-save-source-docs.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Ensures canonical saves include source document references.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"CANONICAL_SAVE_LINEAGE_REQUIRED\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-canonical-save-lineage.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Ensures canonical save lineage metadata is present.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"CANONICAL_SAVE_PACKET_IDENTITY_NORMALIZED\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-canonical-save-packet-identity.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks canonical save packet identity normalization.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"CANONICAL_SAVE_DESCRIPTION_GRAPH_FRESHNESS\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-canonical-save-description-graph-freshness.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Checks generated description/graph freshness for canonical saves.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"CONTINUITY_FRESHNESS\",\n    \"aliases\": [],\n    \"script_path\": \"validation/continuity-freshness.ts\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"strict_only\": true,\n    \"description\": \"Strict-mode freshness check for continuity frontmatter. The rule reports warn by default and escalates to fail under SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS_ENFORCE; the ceiling here has to allow that escalation, since a warn ceiling would silently cap it.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"GENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"GENERATED_METADATA\",\n      \"METADATA_INTEGRITY\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"validation/generated-metadata-integrity.ts\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"structural\",\n    \"strict_only\": true,\n    \"description\": \"Validates description.json and graph-metadata.json through the shared schemas plus path-prefix and status-enum invariants, error under strict behind a grandfather report mode.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"METADATA_DRIFT\",\n      \"SYNOPSIS_DRIFT\"\n    ],\n    \"script_path\": \"validation/generated-metadata-drift.ts\",\n    \"severity\": \"error\",\n    \"category\": \"structural\",\n    \"strict_only\": true,\n    \"description\": \"Re-derives a folder and reports drift between the stored description/causal_summary and the current docs, read-only, error under strict only when the drift-gate flag is on and otherwise grandfather report mode.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule_id\": \"LINKS_VALID\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"WIKILINKS_VALID\",\n      \"CHECK_LINKS\"\n    ],\n    \"category\": \"operational_runtime\",\n    \"description\": \"Scans the system-spec-kit skill's own markdown for wikilinks whose target file does not exist. The target is always this skill, never the validated packet.\",\n    \"script_path\": \"rules/check-links.sh\",\n    \"severity\": \"warn\"\n  }\n]\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"34df13","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
