{"toolCallId":"call_db6e56e014ec4244b291f84d6b296d3e","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"=== spec.md ===\n101:| REQ-007 | With `--quiet`, every warning the script writes to stderr is still written to stderr; `--quiet` trims stdout only. |\n=== tasks.md ===\n53:- [ ] T017 Keep every warning on stderr when `--quiet` is set: the guard trims stdout only and adds no redirect around a stderr write (REQ-007) (recommend-level.sh)\n=== acceptance-criteria.md ===\n64:| AC-011 | REQ-007 | Given a run that writes a warning to stderr and passes `--quiet`, When the script runs, Then the warning still appears on stderr and stdout carries only the level line | Run with stdout and stderr captured separately (`>out 2>err`): `err` holds the warning verbatim, `wc -l` on `out` = 1, and the quiet path contains no `2>&1` or fd-2 redirect | Unmet | - |\n=== graph-metadata derived freshness ===\n{\n  \"last_save_at\": \"2026-10-26T05:22:33.535Z\",\n  \"source_fingerprint\": \"sha256:aa5e6f81b34715c3e381c92e1893c0b8e651c55a12c3c39c530d50f4b7210a76\",\n  \"source_doc_hashes\": {\n    \"spec.md\": \"04da5f3f2a764d6c0936d8ef344e71097ab1dc77cef3bd7e5dc16115325ddc42\",\n    \"plan.md\": \"e2fc57465684561b2b5155d7344fd31aa624a01062ced1f5a311987d13c211a9\",\n    \"tasks.md\": \"8a5f668bf3648812e44766f2029d33daa1dc2cd35bc5ea188c28abb14a227ed7\",\n    \"implementation-summary.md\": \"c2633619b0cf4c5615d1f67e7722e254a113acf05f99f97625f0248770557c74\"\n  },\n  \"status\": \"planned\",\n  \"description_causal\": \"`recommend-level.sh` has no way to emit a single value\"\n}\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"c72afb","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
